    {
      "id": "13777",
      "body": "### What was accomplished\n\n**The core problem we solved:** There was no systematic, repeatable way to convert Zimmermann's Handover web components into PWA Kit React components while staying in sync with the designer's ongoing Figma work. We built that pipeline.\n\n**The pipeline, in order:**\n\n1. `/sync-design-tokens` — reads the Handover design system as the single source of truth and writes it into `overrides/app/theme/foundation/` (tokens, typography, spacing, icon sizes, `zimmTokens.ts`). Also wires font loading and CSS custom property injection into `_app-config`.\n1. `/convert-to-uikit {component`} — converts a single Handover web component to a React component under `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/`. Runs three internal phases: plan → build → register. Each converted component gets a `/uikits` preview page entry for visual verification.\n\n### What is pending\n\n1. **Skills and rules need PR review before merging** All skills and `uikit-components.md` are untracked. Several touch Tier 1 files by nature of what they do (`.claude/rules/` is Tier 1 — `.claude/settings.json`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/rules/` are all frozen). A PR for these needs both squad leads and the Integration lead to approve\n1. **Ongoing designer-sync requirement (process, not code)** The workflow is Figma → Handover → PWA Kit. The designer is actively restructuring Figma to align with Handover patterns. Every time Figma changes produce a Handover update, `/sync-design-tokens` must be re-run, then any affected components re-checked. This is a continuous, active loop — not a one-time task. Close coordination with the designer is required to catch breaking changes before they propagate downstream.\n\n        **The proposed gate:** a component must exist in the Handover before it can be converted in the PWA Kit. This      needs formal lead approval before it becomes a hard requirement in the workflow.\n\n\n\nCC: User:712020:08a6f120-c836-4f71-92db-c97999401c49 User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8",
