    {
      "id": "19064",
      "key": "SFCC-659",
      "summary": "Adyen Composable Storefront Integration — Cartridge &amp; PWA Payment Setup",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Adyen Composable Storefront Integration — Cartridge & PWA Payment Setup\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the full Adyen Composable Storefront integration for Zimmermann's SFCC-owned (domestic) checkout — the \nint_adyen_PWA\n cartridge in zimmermann-sfcc, and the \n@adyen/adyen-salesforce-pwa\n npm package, checkout page overrides, and MRT environment configuration in zimmermann-pwa. It follows a full review of Adyen's official Composable Storefront documentation (docs.adyen.com/plugins/salesforce-commerce-cloud/composable-storefront and its 5 sub-pages) cross-checked against zimmermann-pwa's existing \n.docs/integration/07-adyen.md\n and confirmed PAY-XXX requirements.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nAdyen is the payment provider for all SFCC-owned (domestic) checkout on Zimmermann storefronts: AU, US (domestic), UK, and EU domestic. International checkout (HK, ME, EU international, US international) is owned by Global-e and does not use Adyen at the PWA layer. No live payments can be accepted on any domestic storefront until both the SFCC cartridge and the PWA-side integration are built and configured — this is a go-live blocker for 4 of Zimmermann's 8 sites.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nInstalling the \nint_adyen_PWA\n cartridge into zimmermann-sfcc and importing its site metadata\nConfiguring Adyen as the SFCC payment processor and the webhook-processing scheduled job\nInstalling the \n@adyen/adyen-salesforce-pwa\n npm package into zimmermann-pwa, wiring SSR routes, and building the checkout payment/confirmation/error/redirect pages\nConfiguring the \nAdyenCheckout\n component, PWA locale config, and the checkout back-navigation/error-recovery hooks\nGenerating Adyen API credentials, configuring webhooks, and setting MRT environment variables per environment\nEnabling launch payment methods (Card, PayPal) and the confirmed August 2026 wave (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Klarna for AU/US only)\nBuilding the Zimmermann-confirmed saved-card CVC re-entry (PAY-022) and new-shipping-address CVC component\nReconciling \n07-adyen.md\n's webhook/server-architecture description against the official Adyen docs\nTriggering MuleSoft's Magento Experience API when an order is created — covers both Adyen-approved domestic orders and Global-e-confirmed international orders (OM-002)\nCompleting Adyen's go-live checklist before any environment accepts live payments\nOut of Scope:\nAdyen Giving (donations), Click-to-Pay, Credit Card Installments, Level 2/3 enhanced scheme data — none are confirmed Zimmermann requirements\nSFRA/SiteGenesis migration steps from Adyen's install guide — not applicable; this is a greenfield build with no prior Adyen integration to migrate from\nThe 4 Global-e-owned international sites (ZimmermannHK, ZimmermannME, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannUSIntl) — Adyen is not used at the PWA layer for these, though the MuleSoft order-creation trigger above intentionally covers orders from those sites too\nDependencies\nApple Pay and Google Pay merchant IDs per domain (Zimmermann-owned, per \n07-adyen.md\n open item #1) — required before wallet buttons can be enabled for live payments\nPer-environment Adyen credentials (client key, API key, HMAC key, merchant account ID per region, test vs. live) for Dev/SIT/UAT/Stage/Prod (\n07-adyen.md\n open item #2) — without these, checkout can't be tested against a real Adyen account\nENH-020 Adyen dynamic checkout — hard dependency on Adyen delivering A/B-able dynamic payment-method display; not confirmed buildable end-to-end until Adyen delivery is confirmed\nPAY-022 CVC-on-saved-card Adyen-side configuration, and the new-shipping-address Custom Risk Rule — both Adyen-side, not a PWA build blocker, but required for the fraud logic to actually function\nPAY-047/048/049 fraud-hold scope — Adyen/NewStore-owned; PWA-side display behaviour not yet signed off\nKlarna-specific setup steps are not covered by the Composable Storefront payment-methods page reviewed for this epic — needs separate research into Adyen's dedicated Klarna payment-method documentation before Story 8 can be scoped in full detail\nCoordinate the MuleSoft order-creation trigger story with the Global-e epic's outbound order-notification story (SFCC-424) to confirm no overlap — SFCC-424 is Zimmermann-to-Global-e notifications (dispatch/refund/RMA); the story here is SFCC-to-MuleSoft, a different direction\nAssumptions & Constraints\nAdyen Web SDK v6 (async \nAdyenCheckout\n constructor), Adyen Checkout API v69+, \ncountryCode\n required at init — per \n07-adyen.md\n §2\nCard tokenisation happens inside an Adyen-hosted iframe; PAN/CVV/cardholder name never reach Zimmermann or SFCC infrastructure (SAQ-A PCI scope target — formal confirmation with Adyen still TBC)\n3D Secure 2 is always an inline challenge, never a redirect off checkout\nThis is a greenfield build — no prior SFRA/SiteGenesis Adyen integration exists at Zimmermann to migrate from\nEnv var work spans two repos with different tier models: zimmermann-sfcc has 5 tiers (dev/test/sit/uat/staging, no prod — production is promoted via SFCC replication), zimmermann-pwa has 6 (dev/test/sit/uat/staging/prod, via \nnpm run env\n)\nSFCC-side Business Manager configuration (payment-processor assignment, cartridge path, job scheduling) is authored as committed XML under \ndata/vendor/adyen-metadata/\n and \ndata/core/sites/*/site.xml\n, imported via \nnpm run data:import:vendor\n — not performed as one-off manual Business Manager clicks, consistent with this repo's existing Global-e/Avalara vendor-metadata pattern\nTest Credentials\nFull test card reference (Visa, Mastercard, eftpos, etc.): https://docs.adyen.com/development-resources/test-cards-and-credentials/test-card-numbers\nStandard credit card validation: PAN 4111 1111 1111 1111 (Visa) or 5555 5555 5555 4444 (Mastercard), any future expiry date, any 3-digit CVV",
